# netsurf: import maps (patch 239)
# Generated 2026-10-11
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 238)
#
# <script type="importmap"> was skipped as an unsupported script type, so
# bare specifiers never resolved: github.com's chunks import "react",
# "react-dom" and co. through its map, and failed ("module fetch FAILED
# status=0 react", then "Loading chunk ... failed after 3 retries").
#
#  - html/script.c: an inline script of type importmap goes to
#    js_set_import_map(thread, json, len, document URL) (js.h; a no-op in
#    the "none" engine).
#  - macsurf_qjs.c: the JSON is parsed in the realm (JS_ParseJSON) into
#    the module registry, which already belongs to one navigation and is
#    reset with it: "imports" and "scopes", keys normalized (a URL-like
#    key to its URL), values resolved against the document; a value that
#    is not URL-like is ignored, and when maps merge the first rule for a
#    key wins. qjs_module_resolve_mapped() resolves through it -- the
#    scopes prefixing the importer's URL, most specific first, then
#    "imports"; exact keys, then the longest "prefix/" key -- and replaces
#    the plain resolver in the module normalizer, the static-graph
#    prefetch scanner (160) and the non-blocking import() loader (159).
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-importmap.html (+ JS-importmap-lib.js, -lib2,
# -b, -scoped) IMPORTMAP 4/4 (Chromium 4/4): a bare specifier, a prefix
# rule, a scope, and dynamic import() through the map. github.com: the
# map's 9 imports load; JS errors 6 -> 3.
#
